Hmmmm. I've never had any problems finding out the b/u/c status of an object.
As far as I know, it can be done by
 1. Dropping on any altar.
 2. Seeing if your pet will walk on it (any pet? or just dogs and cats?)
 3. Identify scroll.
 4. In 3.1.x, giving the item to a monster who can use it (but does this work
for things like armour? I've never seen "the helmet sticks to the goblins head"
before.)
I don't find the priests advantage to be all that great. But I guess that's
very much personal opinion.

I don't think that _all_ the abilities of the game should be able to be gained
by rings/level/blessing etc - there has to be some motivation for choosing a
particular character class (apart from starting equipment). Otherwise, all
high level characters become "I've got every single ability" super hero's, and
they all look just the same. I think that implementing this a bit further would
even up the game balance a bit at higher levels for super hacks.

Also, some abilities (like I think, the priest's one discussed here) are
particular to the _class_ - they can do this _because_ they are priests - it's
natural for them. But I guess that it's a magical world and anything can
happen...
